# Line endings are part of a file's identity in this project.
#
# index.html loads every script and stylesheet with a version tag that is a
# hash of that file's contents, so that a browser never serves a stale copy.
# Windows git defaults to rewriting LF into CRLF on checkout — which changes
# the contents, which makes every one of those tags wrong. A fresh clone on
# Windows failed the cache-tag test on all fifty-two files for exactly that
# reason, while the deployed site was fine, because Linux checks out LF.
#
# So: the same bytes everywhere, on every machine.
* text=auto eol=lf
